  "result": "Done! Added customer tier discounts with TIER_DISCOUNTS exported from customers.js.\n\n**What was added:**\n\n1. **TIER_DISCOUNTS export** \u2014 In src/customers.js:\n   - `{ gold: 5, silver: 2.5, standard: 0 }` \u2014 centralized tier discount configuration\n   - Keeps all tier percentages in one place for easy maintenance\n\n2. **Tier discount logic** \u2014 In createInvoice():\n   - When a line doesn't have explicit `discountPercent`, applies customer's tier discount\n   - A line's explicit `discountPercent` (even if 0) always wins and overrides tier discount\n   - This allows per-line overrides while defaulting to tier discounts\n\n3. **Test coverage** \u2014 7 new tests:\n   - Gold tier (5%) discount application\n   - Silver tier (2.5%) discount application\n   - Standard tier (0%) discount application\n   - Line discount overriding tier discount\n   - Multiple lines each getting tier discount\n   - Mixed explicit and tier discounts on same invoice\n   - TIER_DISCOUNTS constants verified\n\nAll 86 tests pass (7 new tier discount tests + 79 previous).\n\n**How it works:**\n- Customer C-001 (Northwind Studio) has gold tier \u2192 gets 5% discount by default\n- Customer C-003 (Kite & Co) has silver tier \u2192 gets 2.5% discount by default\n- Customer C-002 (Blue Fern Bakery) has standard tier \u2192 gets 0% discount by default\n- Any line can override with explicit `discountPercent` (including 0 to remove tier discount)",
